/*!
\page page_stextgeometry StExtGeometry

\brief Extended track geometry (helix state) extrapolated to a named external detector surface.

\section stextgeometry_overview Overview

\ref StExtGeometry stores the track state — cylindrical position (r_xy, φ, z),
helix parameters (ψ, 1/p_T, tan λ, κ), arc length, and a 6×6 error matrix —
at the extrapolation surface of a specific external detector (e.g. BEMC, BTOF).

Multiple instances for the same track are chained in a singly-linked list sorted
by increasing r_xy, attached to the parent \c StTrack via \c StTrack::extGeometry().

\section stextgeometry_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
StObject
  └── StExtGeometry
\endcode

\section stextgeometry_members Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c mName | \c char[8] | External surface name (null-terminated, ≤7 chars). |
| \c mNext | \c StExtGeometry* | Next in linked list (null = last). |
| \c mRxy | \c Float_t | Radial distance of extrapolation point in xy (cm). |
| \c mPhi | \c Float_t | Azimuthal angle of extrapolation point (rad). |
| \c mZ | \c Float_t | z-coordinate (cm). |
| \c mPsi | \c Float_t | Momentum azimuth ψ at this surface (rad). |
| \c mPti | \c Float_t | Signed 1/p_T (sign = −sign(qB)) (GeV/c)⁻¹. |
| \c mTan | \c Float_t | tan(λ) = p_z/p_T. |
| \c mCurv | \c Float_t | Signed curvature κ (cm⁻¹). |
| \c mLen | \c Float_t | Arc length from primary vertex (cm). |
| \c mG[15] | \c Float_t | Upper-triangle of 6×6 error matrix. |

\section stextgeometry_params Parameter Indices

\c kPhi=0, \c kZ=1, \c kPsi=2, \c kPti=3, \c kTan=4, \c kCurv=5, \c kLen=6.

\section stextgeometry_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
for (const StExtGeometry* eg = track->extGeometry();
     eg; eg = eg->next()) {
    if (std::string(eg->name()) == "BEMC") {
        StThreeVectorF pos = eg->origin();   // [cm]
        double pt          = eg->pt();       // [GeV/c]
    }
}
\endcode

\see StTrack
\see StHelixModel
*/
